    {
      "id": "qNuK5czAxg_rkHGVR0CHN",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 313.5352483361295,
      "y": 1954.5124401770936,
      "width": 479.839599609375,
      "height": 1000,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b32",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 918333976,
      "version": 159,
      "versionNonce": 630363752,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783981237760,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n\n-- URL state and UI state drift\nThe filter panel shows one set of values, \nbut the URL represents another.\n== >Mitigation: \nRoute parser produces a single normalized search model.\n\n-- Crawl explosion\nEvery filter combination creates a crawlable URL.\n==> Mitigation: \nCentralized indexability matrix, canonical policy, \nrobots directives, parameter normalization, curated sitemap.\n\n-- Empty indexable pages\nA destination page has no active inventory.\n==> Mitigation: \nInventory thresholds, fallback nearby content, \ntemporary noindex, or retirement workflow.\n\n-- Stale SSR prices\nCached HTML displays a price no longer available.\n==> Mitigation: \nLabel prices as estimates or “from” prices, \nuse conservative cache TTLs, revalidate during booking, \nand avoid exact offers unless freshness is guaranteed.\n\n-- Hydration mismatch\nServer and client use different locale, \ncurrency, dates, or experiment state.\n==> Mitigation: \nSerialize normalized request context into the initial document\n and hydrate from it.\n\nSoft 404s\nRemoved listings return 200 with “Listing unavailable.”\n==> Mitigation: \nDefine explicit lifecycle states and proper redirect, \n404, or 410 behavior.\n\n-- Mobile content parity failure\nSEO copy and links exist only on desktop.\n==> Mitigation: \nResponsive shared DOM and mobile parity tests.\n\n-- Bot-specific rendering drift\nCrawler HTML differs materially from user HTML.\n==> Mitigation: \nOne rendering architecture; avoid bot-only dynamic \nrendering except as a migration bridge.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n\n-- URL state and UI state drift\nThe filter panel shows one set of values, \nbut the URL represents another.\n== >Mitigation: \nRoute parser produces a single normalized search model.\n\n-- Crawl explosion\nEvery filter combination creates a crawlable URL.\n==> Mitigation: \nCentralized indexability matrix, canonical policy, \nrobots directives, parameter normalization, curated sitemap.\n\n-- Empty indexable pages\nA destination page has no active inventory.\n==> Mitigation: \nInventory thresholds, fallback nearby content, \ntemporary noindex, or retirement workflow.\n\n-- Stale SSR prices\nCached HTML displays a price no longer available.\n==> Mitigation: \nLabel prices as estimates or “from” prices, \nuse conservative cache TTLs, revalidate during booking, \nand avoid exact offers unless freshness is guaranteed.\n\n-- Hydration mismatch\nServer and client use different locale, \ncurrency, dates, or experiment state.\n==> Mitigation: \nSerialize normalized request context into the initial document\n and hydrate from it.\n\nSoft 404s\nRemoved listings return 200 with “Listing unavailable.”\n==> Mitigation: \nDefine explicit lifecycle states and proper redirect, \n404, or 410 behavior.\n\n-- Mobile content parity failure\nSEO copy and links exist only on desktop.\n==> Mitigation: \nResponsive shared DOM and mobile parity tests.\n\n-- Bot-specific rendering drift\nCrawler HTML differs materially from user HTML.\n==> Mitigation: \nOne rendering architecture; avoid bot-only dynamic \nrendering except as a migration bridge.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
